desc.grep.ripgrep=Search file contents with ripgrep (rg). `pattern` is a Rust regular expression (backreferences and lookaround are not supported); set `literal: true` for plain text. Respects `.gitignore`/`.ignore` and skips hidden files unless `path` names one. `glob` is a gitignore-style filter passed to `--glob`. Output is `path:line:text` with an optional context window; lines are capped at 500 characters.
desc.grep.grep=Search file contents with the system grep (POSIX extended regex: no `\d` classes, no lazy quantifiers); set `literal: true` for plain text. Ignored and hidden files are searched (`.git` is skipped best-effort); binary files are skipped. `glob` is a shell-style file-name filter passed to `--include`. Output is `path:line:text` with an optional context window; lines are capped at 500 characters.
desc.grep.builtin=Search file contents with a literal string or a small regex (., *, +, ?, ^, $, [abc], [^abc], \ escapes). Output is path:line:text with an optional context window; lines are capped at 500 characters. (built-in engine)
desc.find.fd=Find files whose path or name matches a glob pattern (`*`, `?`, `**`, `[abc]`). Uses fd: respects `.gitignore`, skips hidden entries and does not follow symlinked directories. Output is one path per line.
desc.find.posix=Find files with the system find. Pattern translation is approximate (`**` may not match zero directories; a pattern with `/` is matched with `-path` against the path as printed by find, so under the default `.` a root-relative pattern may not match); `.gitignore` and hidden files are not skipped. Output is one path per line.
desc.find.builtin=Find files whose path or name matches a glob pattern (*, ?, **, [abc]). Respects .gitignore files, does not follow symlinked directories and is bounded to 8000 visited entries. (built-in engine)
argv.rg.full=rg --json --ignore-case --glob *.c --context 2 --max-count 6 -- foo .
argv.rg.full=1
argv.rg.literal=rg --json -F --max-count 101 -- -bar .
argv.rg.literal=1
argv.grep.full=grep -r -n -H -I -E -i --include *.c -C 2 --exclude-dir .git -m 6 -- foo .
argv.grep.full=1
argv.grep.portable=1
argv.grep.literal=grep -r -n -H -I -F --exclude-dir .git -m 101 -- bar .
argv.grep.literal=1
argv.grep.null=grep -r -n -H -Z -I -E --exclude-dir .git -m 101 -- foo .
argv.grep.null=1
argv.fd.full=fd --glob --max-results 6 -- *.c src
argv.fd.full=1
argv.fd.default=fd --glob --max-results 1001 -- *.c .
